ution emerged during a critical period characterized by the Cold War, economic uncertainties, and the need for collaborative policy-making in an increasingly interdependent world. Its inception was marked by the involvement of influential leaders such as former U.S. National Security Advisor Zbigniew Brzezinski and former Canadian Prime Minister Pierre Trudeau, who sought to address the complex global challenges of the time.

